# O1 of the engine modularization plan (docs/engine/modularization_plan.md, section 3.1): okayui/src/OkayUI.cpp split by widget
# family. Four commits, each checked on its own against the commit before it:
#   1. OkayUIInternal.hpp: the shared state and helpers the moved code needs (the structs and small inline helpers move there;
#      the variables get an `extern` line and the functions a prototype, their definitions stay in OkayUI.cpp)
#   2. OkayUI_Tooltips.cpp (tooltips: Tooltip, SetTooltip, BeginTooltip / EndTooltip, the pending-tooltip flush)
#   3. OkayUI_DrawList.cpp (the public draw list: shapes, paths, textured polygons, the window and foreground lists)
#   4. OkayUI_Tables.cpp (columns and tables)
#   python3 scripts/check_pure_move.py --base <commit before> --head <commit> --source okayui/src/OkayUI.cpp \
#       --dest okayui/src/OkayUIInternal.hpp (commit 1; --dest okayui/src/OkayUI_<Family>.cpp for commits 2 to 4) \
#       --rules docs/engine/moves/O1_okayui_split.rules
# Part 2 (OkayUI_Menus.cpp: menu bar, menus, selectables, popups, combo, popup queries; OkayUI_Windows.cpp: windows, children, scrolling, window
# queries): three more commits, the same check. Step 1 moves the structs and small inline helpers they read into the header (they keep `inline`),
# adds `extern` lines and prototypes, and edits the definition lines of the file-static window state (`static` left, `ui_core::` added). The rules of
# part 2 are at the end of this file.
# The edits that are not moves: the toolkit's old anonymous namespace of state (and the few later blocks that hold state the new
# files read) became `namespace ui_core`, so the new files reach it through the header; every file that uses it says
# `using namespace ui_core;`. Where a function had to be reachable, `static` / `inline` left its definition (one drop and one add
# rule below per function) and default arguments moved to the prototype in the header. The rules below were generated from the
# pristine file by a script and are exactly the allowed edits; the extern lines and prototypes are listed one by one.
